# Family Values (AtroUI)

Inspired by [Family Values](https://benji.org/family-values). Every product UI change in this repo should respect these principles. Table-stakes (utility, performance, security, a11y, `prefers-reduced-motion`) are never traded away.

## Simplicity — gradual revelation

- Fundamentals stay visible; depth appears when relevant.
- Prefer overlays / trays / progressive disclosure over dumping every option on screen.
- One primary action or idea per focused surface (tray, dialog step, hero scrap).
- Keep context: overlay on place rather than full-screen teleport when the user is mid-task.

## Fluidity — fly, don’t teleport

- Transitions must clarify path A→B (space, direction, cause).
- Shared elements that persist should **travel**, not remount as duplicates.
- Prefer short tweens (`easeOutExpo`-ish) over spring overshoot for chrome (drawers, menus) — overshoot feels glitchy on web.
- Directional motion for hierarchical nav; lateral/fade for peer switches.
- Fixed overlays: portal to `document.body`, iOS-safe scroll lock (`apps/docs/hooks/use-body-scroll-lock.ts`), shared easings (`apps/docs/lib/motion.ts`).
- Never animate “for vibes” without an architectural reason.

## Delight — selective emphasis

- Polish everywhere; sprinkle magic selectively.
- Frequent paths: tiny details only (copy feedback, label morph, comma shift energy).
- Rare paths: stronger moments allowed (settling chalk, confetti-scale only if earned).
- Corners count (empty states, errors, 404) — dirty bathroom problem.
- Avoid AI-slop atmosphere: no soft blur-orb soup as the product identity. Prefer intentional material (chalkboard, real WebGL sphere, owned sketch language).

## When editing UI

1. Name which principle you’re serving.
2. Prefer shared motion tokens over one-off springs.
3. Respect reduced motion: skip decorative motion; keep clarity.
4. Mobile is first-class — no “CSS bloom only” excuses that leave a lifeless frame.
